From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: fwnode: fix uninitialized detection flags on O6N

On O6N (CIX Sky1) the ACPI-declared regulators gbe, cam, etc. produced a
burst of ~8 boot warnings from the regulator core:

  gbe: IC does not support requested under-voltage limits
  gbe: IC does not support requested over-current limits
  gbe: IC does not support requested over-voltage limits
  gbe: IC does not support requested temperature limits
  (and the same four for cam)

The warnings come from set_machine_constraints() in the regulator core:
when a constraint's *_detection flag is set but the backing regulator
driver has no matching set_*_protection op, handle_notify_limits() returns
-EOPNOTSUPP and the core warns. gbe/cam are simple board rails whose ACPI
description declares no oc/ov/uv/temp notification limits at all, so those
detection flags should never have been set.

Root cause is in the CIX fwnode/ACPI constraint parser
fwnode_get_regulator_prot_limits(): unlike its upstream twin in
of_regulator.c (of_get_regulator_prot_limits), it declared

	bool found;			/* never initialized */
	...
	ret = fwnode_property_read_u32(np, prop, &pval);
	if (!ret) {
		fill_limit(l[j], pval);
		found = true;		/* only ever set true, never false */
	}
	set[i] |= found;		/* reads stale/garbage 'found' */

'found' is used uninitialized on the first level of every property class
and is never cleared when a property is absent, so set[i] gets OR'd with
stack garbage (or a stale 'true' from an earlier class). That spuriously
raises over_current/over_voltage/over_temp/under_voltage_detection for
rails that declared none of them, and the core then warns four times per
such rail.

Fix it to mirror the upstream of_regulator.c form: assign 'found' from the
property read at the top of every level so it is true only when that exact
property is present, false otherwise. Detection flags now reflect what the
ACPI table actually declares, and the eight spurious warnings disappear.
This is a genuine bug fix in the CIX ACPI constraint path, not a message
demotion. The now-unused 'ret' local is dropped.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/fwnode_regulator.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 				struct regulation_constraints *constraints)
 {
 	u32 pval;
-	int i, ret;
+	int i;
 	static const char *const props[] = {
 		"regulator-oc-%s-microamp",
 		"regulator-ov-%s-microvolt",
@@ -64,11 +64,9 @@

 		for (j = 0; j < ARRAY_SIZE(lvl); j++) {
 			snprintf(prop, 255, props[i], lvl[j]);
-			ret = fwnode_property_read_u32(np, prop, &pval);
-			if (!ret) {
+			found = !fwnode_property_read_u32(np, prop, &pval);
+			if (found)
 				fill_limit(l[j], pval);
-				found = true;
-			}
 			set[i] |= found;
 		}
 	}
